          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कटना (kaṭnā) is the intransitive partner of काटना, both from Sanskrit kartati, \"cuts\" (CDIAL 2854), which lists Hindi kaṭnā, \"to be cut\". A side road कटती where it cuts away from the main one."
